Teams
Solo or teams of up to 5. Only registered teammates in indieconnect will get Tickets upon winning.
Registration closes before the event starts. Members cannot swap teams or join more than one team.
At least the POC member must be in the event Discord server with the Discord username they registered.
On Discord, pick your team role (⁠join-teams ). If it does not exist yet, create a private thread named after your team under ⁠join-teams .
Need help? Ping the Admin TGC role.
UG1 Track is only for teams where every member is an IIITH UG or PG 2026 batch student. Anyone from anywhere in the world can participate in the General Track

Proposal and concept lock
Mentors help you shape your idea from Hour 0 until Hour 12.
Hour 12 (hard): submit your final scope, public GitHub repository and final idea through the official form. No major premise pivots after this. Evaluation compares your game against this plan.

Fresh codebase
All game code, mechanics and core architecture must be built within the 100 hours.
Allowed: generic engine starter templates and small open source features, for example a standard Godot character controller or the Unity default scene.
Banned, with immediate disqualification: complete game starter kits, full game templates, prebuilt system logic, pre existing games and copy pasted projects.
Keep a public GitHub repository with a proper license. Commit history is audited.
 
@everyone, Assets
Paid third party assets are forbidden (Unity Asset Store, Unreal Marketplace, paid itch.io assets, Fab, private marketplaces).
Only free, open source, AI generated or Creative Commons (CC0, CC BY) audio, textures, 3D models and fonts are allowed.
List every third party asset in CREDITS.md in the repository root and on the itch.io page, with source links and licenses.

AI tools
AI tools are allowed and must be fully disclosed: LLMs for code or text, and image, sound or 3D generators.
Core design and direction must show your own effort.

Final submission (Hour 100)
Strict code freeze. Code is pulled at the deadline. Backdating on GitHub or itch.io means disqualification.
A public browser playable (HTML5 or WebGL) build on itch.io.
The root README.md must show the itch.io link, setup and run instructions, controls and team details.
Deliver a complete, stable gameplay loop of 10 to 15 minutes. Playtime beyond 20 minutes (average first playthrough) is not evaluated.

Disqualification from the prize pool
Missing public source code or an on time itch.io playable build, using paid assets, writing game code before Hour 0 or authorship that cannot be backed up.

Communication
Official announcements, team check ins and mentor communication run only through the event Discord server.

Decisions
Judging panel and organising committee decisions on rule interpretation, disqualifications and scores are final. Results are published within one week of the event.

